## COMMUNICATION
A copper-phthalocyanine-based 2D conjugated MOF with square planar cobalt-bis(dihydroxy) complexes (CoO4) as linkages is developed as electrocatalyst for oxygen reduction reaction with high catalytic activity $(\mathsf{E}_{1/2}\mathrm{=}\ 0.83\ \vee$ vs. RHE). Linkage Co centers with optimised electronic structure $(\mathsf{e}_{\mathfrak{g}}{=}1)$ are identified as active sites.
